window.docContents[2].resolve({"/Gamma-Function/___5___13-Integrals/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--___5___13-Integrals--___5___13_LPAR_ii_RPAR_-Ramanujan___s-Beta-Integral":{"contents":"\\[\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}t}{\\Gamma(a+t)\\Gamma(b+t)\\Gamma(c-t)\\Gamma(d-t)}\n=\\frac{\\Gamma(a+b+c+d-3)}\n{\\Gamma(a+c-1)\\Gamma(a+d-1)\\Gamma(b+c-1)\\Gamma(b+d-1)},\\qquad\n\\Re(a+b+c+d)>3.\\]The reciprocal Gamma product is integrated ordinarily over the real line.  The source\nrequires only the displayed real-part inequality on the sum.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Gamma Function\u0009§5.13 Integrals","header":"§5.13(ii) Ramanujan's Beta Integral","id":"/Gamma-Function/___5___13-Integrals/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--___5___13-Integrals--___5___13_LPAR_ii_RPAR_-Ramanujan___s-Beta-Integral"}});